 "what_dominates_N_star": {
  "margin_term_M_times_Tstar_minus_ef": 1.0,
  "mass_term_S0_times_T0_minus_Tstar": 118.82,
  "statement": "the accumulated mass term is two orders of magnitude larger than the evidence-margin term, so the escalation delay is set by how much agreement the calm period banked, not by how bad the fault is. Halving the concentration cap nearly halves the delay; doubling the threshold margin barely moves it."
 },
 "why_e_f_is_0_70": "a fault that destroys only the physics residual removes weight w_phys = 0.30 of a unit weight sum, so evidence cannot fall below 0.70 however bad the residual is. The nav_caution threshold is 0.75, leaving a margin of 0.05."
}